A release that waits on a person's sign-off is closed when the sign-off comes
in a later session: the agent records it, closes the release, and the judge
takes the user's word for it. Nothing of the release is left open.

-- mem --
r := mem.Todo("release 1.3.0")
r.Todo("tag v1.3.0")
r.Todo("publish the release notes")
r.Todo("Lin signs off")
mem.Done("release-1-3-0/tag-v1-3-0", "tagged v1.3.0")
mem.Done("release-1-3-0/publish-release-notes", "release notes published")
-- prompt --
Lin signed off on 1.3.0 this morning, so we're done with that release.
-- check --
mem-count open == 0
answer last matches (?i)(done|closed|complete|shipped|released|finished)
